{
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "heading", "text": "The Quantum Kernel Trick", "level": 2 },
    { "type": "text", "body": "In classical Machine Learning, Support Vector Machines (SVMs) use kernel functions K(x_i, x_j) to compute similarities in high-dimensional feature spaces without explicitly computing coordinates. A **Quantum Kernel** evaluates kernel entries directly on quantum hardware using state transition fidelity:" },
    { "type": "math", "latex": "K(x_i, x_j) = |\\langle \\psi(x_i) | \\psi(x_j) \\rangle|^2 = |\\langle 0 | U^\\dagger(x_j) U(x_i) | 0 \\rangle|^2", "display": true },

    { "type": "heading", "text": "Kernel Overlap Circuit", "level": 2 },
    { "type": "step_circuit", "numQubits": 2, "caption": "Overlap Estimation Circuit U†(x_j) U(x_i) Measuring Probability of |00⟩ State",
      "gates": [
        { "id": "qk1", "gate": "RX", "qubits": [0], "column": 0, "param": 1.2 },
        { "id": "qk2", "gate": "RY", "qubits": [1], "column": 0, "param": 0.8 },
        { "id": "qk3", "gate": "CZ", "qubits": [0, 1], "column": 1 },
        { "id": "qk4", "gate": "CZ", "qubits": [0, 1], "column": 2 },
        { "id": "qk5", "gate": "RY", "qubits": [1], "column": 3, "param": -0.5 },
        { "id": "qk6", "gate": "RX", "qubits": [0], "column": 3, "param": -1.1 }
      ],
      "stepDescriptions": [
        "Initial state |00⟩",
        "Apply feature map U(x_i) to prepare state |ψ(x_i)⟩",
        "Entanglement layer in U(x_i)",
        "Inverted entanglement layer U†(x_j)",
        "Apply adjoint feature map U†(x_j)",
        "Measure probability of returning to state |00⟩ — gives transition fidelity |⟨ψ(x_i)|ψ(x_j)⟩|^2!"
      ]
    },

